wearable_pipeline/pupil.py was developed with reference to, and checked line by
line against, the MATLAB code accompanying

  Kret, M. E., & Sjak-Shie, E. E. (2019). Preprocessing pupil size data:
  Guidelines and code. Behavior Research Methods, 51, 1336-1342.
  https://github.com/ElioS-S/pupil-size (GPL-3.0)

Changes from that code (October and November 2026):
  - rewritten in Python, for two eyes sampled on one clock;
  - blink events plus 500 ms, and off-head samples, set to missing;
  - the isolated-island filter is not implemented;
  - a single eye is shifted by half the mean between-eye difference;
  - the range gate defaults to 1.5-9 mm, with 1-9 mm as a sensitivity.
The authors of that code have not reviewed or endorsed this one.
